    "approved_definition_context": [
      "NNReal denotes nonnegative reals; upward arrows are real coercions. Module.finrank is real vector-space dimension. ContDiff R 2 is C2 regularity. fderiv and gradient are genuine Frechet and inner-product derivatives in the displayed spatial argument.",
      "Kernel S X is a measurable family of measures on X indexed by S; IsMarkovKernel means every fiber is a probability. Measure.map is pushforward. Measure.prod is product measure. Measure.infinitePi is the countable product measure with the given coordinate laws. Nested products associate right.",
      "stdGaussian E is the centered Gaussian probability with identity covariance. volume is canonical real volume. volume.restrict(Ioc 0 1) is Lebesgue measure restricted to(0,1]; Icc 0 1 is[0,1]. poissonMeasure of a nonnegative real is the Poisson probability with that mean. A Fin n index runs from0 to n-1, with empty product equal to1 when n=0. Every displayed acceptance product is indexed by Fin of that attempt batch-size coordinate, even when the pretty-printer only displays the product index name.",
      "A measure tilted f is exponential tilting by exp(f), normalized using the integral and Mathlib total-inverse conventions. This is a definition of a measure, not an implicit integrability premise. mu.rnDeriv nu is the extended nonnegative Radon-Nikodym derivative of mu with respect to nu; toReal is the standard real conversion, with infinity sent to0. The notation mu absolutelyContinuous nu means every nu-null measurable set is mu-null.",
      "ENNReal is the extended nonnegative reals. ENNReal.ofReal(r)=max(r,0). The integral with superscript minus is nonnegative extended integration. Integrable denotes Bochner integrability, including almost-everywhere strong measurability and finite norm integral. An ordinary integral uses Mathlib total Bochner conventions. Equality with superscript m relative to a measure means almost-everywhere equality. A tsum is a countable sum.",
      "Function iteration T^[n] includes identity at n=0. Nat.find takes the least natural satisfying the supplied existential witness. A dependent if may use that witness in its selected branch. A displayed have inside a type is a local let binding. Real inverse,division,sqrt and logarithm are total functions under Mathlib conventions. The context explains notation only and does not supply source identity, additional hypotheses or extra conclusions."
    ]
